      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I don’t understand why the world isn’t secondary information if it’s a list of people. 🤔 it says “friends” not “locations” at the top.\n\nThis is totally confusing to skim. And the OP is right. The cognitive load is high. Especially with the introduced visual noise of nameplate art.\n\nEDIT: if this changes based on sort type. Then my comment about the primary info makes no sense. But the readability could still be improved, as this canny suggests.",
